scripts/rebase-push.md:3:`scripts/rebase-push.sh` is the canonical "rebase onto latest base" primitive used at every freshness checkpoint in `/implement` (Steps 1.m, 1.r, 4.r, 7.r, 7a.r, 8b, the Rebase + Re-bump Sub-procedure invoked from Steps 8b/10/12, and the conflict-resolution Phase 4 path) and at `/design` Step 1's pre-implementation rebase. By default it fetches `origin/main`, runs `git rebase origin/main`, and (unless `--no-push`) force-pushes with lease. Callers may override the base with `--base-remote NAME --base-ref BRANCH`; `/implement --forked` uses `upstream/main`.

