docs/issue-anchored-plan.md:245:**Plan probe placement**: `/fix-issue` PR work gates on `find-lock-issue.sh --require-plan-block`, which delegates to `plan-block-read.sh` before the `IN PROGRESS` lock. Direct `/implement` reads the same markers in **Preflight** via `plan-block-read.sh`; Step 1 only copies the already-extracted plan from the Preflight tmpdir into `$IMPLEMENT_TMPDIR/plan.txt` — it does not substitute a separate literal `/fix-issue` Step 4a sequence inside `/implement`.
docs/linting.md:181:| `make test-wait-for-reviewers` | Run the wait/collector regression harness. Pins `scripts/wait-for-reviewers.sh`'s `--timeout` rejection contract (exit 1 + stderr `must be a positive integer` for `0` / `00` / `000` / non-numeric, `--timeout requires a value` for missing arg), `WAIT_FOR_REVIEWERS_POLL_INTERVAL=00` / `000` rejection, and the indexed `DONE <idx> <basename>` / `TIMEOUT <idx> <basename>` stdout grammar; also covers the collector's wait-passthrough fix from #1188 (collector `--timeout 0` / `abc` exits 1 with no `STATUS=` records). A `make lint` prerequisite via the `test-harnesses-N` shard partition. |
docs/linting.md:190:| `make test-analyze` | Run the behavioral regression harness for `.claude/skills/analyze-issues/scripts/analyze.py`. Exercises `.claude/skills/analyze-issues/scripts/test-analyze.sh` against the checked-in `test-fixture.json` (10 minimal issues covering Tracking/umbrella, `[OOS]` prefix stripping, Bug fix, Test coverage (without `fix`-in-`fixture` aliasing), Documentation/contract drift via the explicit `documentation` keyword (the fixture row body uses `Documentation`; the kw list also enumerates `documented` / `documenting` for inflectional coverage in real-world dumps, though no fixture row exercises those forms today) and the `\bdoc\b` whole-word boundary that prevents `Docker` from aliasing as Documentation, Hardening/validation/security, Refactor/code clarity, Other (the `prefix handling tweak` row that pins absence of `fix`-in-`prefix` aliasing), `[STALLED]` (W3), duplicate-titled (W1), and one issue with a `- **Reviewer**:` + `Vote tally: YES=N NO=M` block) plus inline temp fixtures that exercise `load_issues` non-dict and malformed-number handling (stderr per-skip warnings, the unified >5% threshold abort, `--lenient` recovery, rejection of missing/null/non-numeric/unicode/zero/negative/bool numbers, acceptance of ASCII digit strings, and a W4/W5 no-`#0` collapse check). Pins section headers, category labels (with `Bug fix: 3 (`, `Test coverage: 1 (`, `Other: 1 (`, `Documentation/contract drift: 2 (` covering the word-boundary + stem regex and the `Docker`-not-Documentation guard), the auto-spawned `[OOS]` share, the W1 duplicate pair, the W3 stalled count, the reviewer attribution + per-tool/persona aggregation, and the longest-first `codex`/`code` regex alternation (negative assertion that `codex` is not collapsed to `code`). A `make lint` prerequisite via the `test-harnesses-N` shard partition. |
docs/linting.md:249:| `make test-restore-finalize-state` | Run the offline regression harness for `scripts/restore-finalize-state.sh`. Covers missing, partial, and complete `ship-pr-state.sh` inputs, idempotent finalize-state rewrites, `DESIGN_ONLY_DONE=false` defaulting, and final-bail-reason restoration. A `make lint` prerequisite via the `test-harnesses-N` shard partition. |
skills/research/references/citation-validation-phase.md:38:See `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/skills/research/scripts/validate-citations.md` for the full contract (argv, exit codes, sidecar schema, SSRF defenses, regex tiers, idempotency rerun semantics, budget-exhaustion process-group kill — Linux `setsid` available: `kill -- -$$` gated on `__VC_SETSID_DONE=1`; Linux `setsid` absent: per-PID `kill` over `CURL_PIDS` with no `kill -- -$$` because the validator is not a session leader on that branch (issue #779); macOS `set -m` + per-background `kill -- -<pid>` with no `kill -- -$$` fallback because that would self-signal the validator).
skills/research/references/citation-validation-phase.md:134:When the overall validator budget elapses (`--budget-seconds`, default 300), in-flight curl HEAD fetches MUST be terminated cleanly — orphaned curl processes can outlive the validator and skew network telemetry. On Linux when `setsid` is available, the script self-execs into a new session if not already a session leader and a single `kill -- -$$` sweeps every descendant; the kill is gated on `__VC_SETSID_DONE=1` (the dedicated-session marker). When `setsid` is absent from PATH the re-exec is skipped and the timeout handler falls back to per-PID `kill "$pid"` over `CURL_PIDS` so the validator does not self-signal in its caller's process group (issue #779; orphan curls bounded by `$PER_FETCH_TIMEOUT`). macOS `setsid` is non-portable, so the script enables `set -m` (job control) which places each backgrounded `fetch_url` subshell in its own process group; on timeout the script signals each recorded `$!` via `kill -- -<pid>` (terminating the subshell + curl substitution + descendants together). `kill -- -$$` is **not** used as a Darwin fallback: with `set -m` active, `$$`'s process group still contains the validator itself, so signaling it would kill the script before it writes the per-claim `UNKNOWN(timeout)` rows and the sidecar — exit 143, sidecar absent, fail-soft contract broken. The OS detection branch lives in `validate-citations.sh`; the macOS path is asserted by Test 20 in `test-validate-citations.sh` (Darwin-only — exercised on developer macOS), and the Linux no-setsid path is asserted by Test 21 (Linux-only, issue #849 — exercised by current Ubuntu CI; runs when `setsid` is available on the runner so the harness can isolate the validator in its own session).
skills/research/scripts/test-validate-citations-budget.md:12:| Linux no-setsid budget exhaustion (Test 21, Linux-only, #849) | outer `setsid -w` wraps the validator in its own session; hermetic clean-bin (symlinks excluding `setsid`, including `uname`) makes `command -v setsid` fail inside the validator so the no-setsid branch (`validate-citations.sh:765`) is exercised; hung fake-curl honoring `--max-time` + `--budget-seconds 1` -> exit 0, sidecar present, `UNKNOWN`/`timeout` rows for both hung URLs, no orphan fake-curl PIDs after the shortened `--per-fetch-timeout` window. Runs when `setsid` is available on the runner PATH; otherwise skipped with note. Demonstrably fails if the `__VC_SETSID_DONE` marker gate at `validate-citations.sh:765` is reverted to unconditional `kill -- -$$` (validator gets SIGTERM under outer setsid -> exit 143). Test 21 is exercised by current Ubuntu CI. |
