scripts/test-wait-for-reviewers.md:7:- **R4, R5** (stdout grammar): `^DONE <idx> <basename>: exit=<code>$` on success, `^TIMEOUT <idx> <basename>$` on missed sentinel. This is the grammar that `scripts/collect-agent-results.sh`'s index-keyed timeout parser depends on.
scripts/test-wait-for-reviewers.md:8:- **R6** (duplicate basename fixture): two sentinel paths under different directories share `same.done` but emit distinct `DONE 1 same` / `DONE 2 same` records.
scripts/test-wait-for-reviewers.md:10:- **S1** (suspend-delta detection): PATH-stubbed `date` reports a long poll iteration and PATH-stubbed `sleep` materializes the sentinel during that iteration. The harness asserts the reviewer still reports `DONE` and diagnostics contain `suspend detected`.
scripts/check-clean-tree.md:44:- `skills/fix-issue/scripts/find-lock-issue.sh` calls `--fail-closed` immediately before issue-lock acquisition, so dirty trees abort before `GO` deletion, `IN PROGRESS` comments, or title renames.
